node_modules
dist
build

**/node_modules
**/build
**/dist

packages/server/.env
packages/ui/.env

# Never ship any .env into an image. The three above were the only ones listed;
# a fourth anywhere in the tree would have been copied in silently.
.env
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/.env.*.local

# Local databases and secrets must never enter the build context either.
#
# This list MUST stay in step with the secret section of .gitignore, .prettierignore
# and .eslintrc.js ignorePatterns (AGENTS.md §9). It was NOT: the root Dockerfile does
# `COPY . .`, and a real production credential export (flowise-credentials-backup-*.json,
# root-owned 0600) sits in the working directory. Excluded from git and the linters but
# NOT here, it would have entered the build context and baked into an image layer under
# `COPY . .` — and a Docker Hub push would have published production credentials. The
# Dockerfile now also asserts no such artifact reached the image, as defense in depth.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.keys
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/*.keystore
**/*.jks
# Credential exports and database dumps (the real leak that motivated this block).
flowise-credentials-backup-*.json
*credentials-backup*
# Private keys and cloud service-account material.
**/id_rsa
**/id_dsa
**/id_ecdsa
**/id_ed25519
**/*service-account*.json
**/*secret*.json
# Any .env variant, keeping the example templates.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
# Config backups that may embed secrets (e.g. compose/nginx snapshots).
**/*.bak
**/*.bak-*

# Maintainer material, not runtime material.
#
# upstream-archive/ is 71 MB of upstream pull requests, issues, advisories and
# discussions captured before the 2026-08-10 archival. It has no business in a
# runtime image on size alone -- and 15 of the 347 archived patches carry diff
# hunks against packages/server/src/enterprise/ and IdentityManager.ts, because
# that is what those community PRs changed. Copying it in put fragments of
# commercially licensed source into the image.
upstream-archive
.git
.github
.githooks
